error[ffi_field_type]: `Tagged.name` is `char[16]` in `ffi-a-cstr-field-blames-the-field.h`, not `cstr` — clang read the header's struct and the field disagrees
  at tests/golden/unsupported/ffi-a-cstr-field-blames-the-field.hero:33:9
     |
  33 |         name: cstr  #~ ffi_field_type
     |         ^^^^
  note: a group's `record` IS the header's struct (§4.19), so every field is at the header's own width and sign: correct `name`, or name the header that spells `Tagged` this way
  note: where the header writes `char`, the field is `i8`: C's `char` is signed in every build, which passes `-fsigned-char`
  fix (guess): declare `name` with `i8[16]`
